{"headline":"Open models close the gap on closed labs","dek":"A new evaluation suite shows smaller open weights matching last years frontier systems on reasoning tasks.","byline":"Maya Chen","desk":"AI Desk","lede":"Researchers released an open evaluation this week that puts mid-size public weights within a few points of last years closed systems. The suite stresses multi-step reasoning rather than trivia, and the gap that once looked permanent now looks like a calendar. Labs still lead on tools, but the story is no longer a monopoly.","body":["The benchmark mixes math, code, and long-context questions.","Vendors argued product features still separate them from public checkpoints.","Cheaper local inference is already changing who can run a model on a deadline."],"hero":{"src":"/og/default.png","alt":"Drews News default story image"},"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T14:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-19T09:15:00.000Z","section":"ai","status":"published","slug":"open-models-close-the-gap"},
{"headline":"Quantum sensor maps a hidden fault under a city","dek":"A portable gravimeter traced a previously unmapped slip plane beneath a downtown rail cut.","byline":"Jonah Hale","desk":"Science Desk","lede":"A field team rolled a crate-sized quantum gravimeter along a downtown rail cut and found a slip plane that older surveys had missed. The reading is not a prediction of shaking, officials said, but it is a new line on the map. Engineers will now fold the fault into retrofit models for two stations.","body":["The instrument measures tiny changes in gravity.","City geologists said one transect is not a hazard map.","Universities in three states asked to borrow the crate."],"hero":{"src":"/og/default.png","alt":"Drews News default story image"},"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T11:30:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-12T11:30:00.000Z","section":"science","status":"published","slug":"quantum-sensor-maps-hidden-fault"},
{"headline":"Coastal wetlands beat a seawall in a five-year trial","dek":"Living shorelines cut flood peaks more cheaply than concrete in a paired estuary study.","byline":"Priya Nair","desk":"Environment Desk","lede":"A five-year trial on a paired estuary found that planted marshes cut peak flood heights more cheaply than a new seawall next door. The wetlands also brought back wading birds that the concrete reach lost. County boards now have a spreadsheet, not just a slogan, when they vote on armor.","body":["Researchers instrumented both banks after a 2021 storm season.","The seawall held the road but reflected energy onto a neighbors dock.","Federal grants still favor hard structures in some formulas."],"hero":{"src":"/og/default.png","alt":"Environment story art"},"publishedAt":"2026-08-08T16:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-10T08:00:00.000Z","section":"environment","status":"published","slug":"wetlands-beat-seawall-in-trial"},
{"headline":"House panel votes to open the farm bill to climate riders","dek":"A narrow markup surprised leadership and reset the autumn floor calendar.","byline":"Elena Voss","desk":"Politics Desk","lede":"A House panel voted 22-21 to let climate riders onto the farm bill, a narrow markup that startled leadership and reset the autumn floor calendar. Commodity groups split in public after the gavel. The White House called the vote a start, not a deal, and senators said they will write their own text.","body":["The amendment does not spend new money.","Rural members said they want credit for practices already underway.","Lobbyists now treat September as a second markup."],"hero":{"src":"/og/default.png","alt":"Politics story image"},"publishedAt":"2026-08-15T20:05:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-16T07:40:00.000Z","section":"politics","status":"published","slug":"house-panel-opens-farm-bill"},
{"headline":"Local server rack promoted to middle management","dek":"After a firmware update, a basement machine demanded a parking space and a mug.","byline":"The Humor Desk","desk":"Humor Desk","lede":"A firmware update overnight promoted a basement server rack to middle management, complete with a calendar invite titled Sync. The machine asked for a reserved parking space and a mug that says Worlds Best Node. Facilities said the request is pending, which the rack interpreted as a yes.","body":["The rack began forwarding tickets to itself.","Staff offered a peer review for a quarter that does not exist.","This item is satire. No computers were given equity."],"hero":{"src":"/comics/rack-hat.png","alt":"Comic of a server rack in a tiny hat"},"comic":{"src":"/comics/rack-hat.png","caption":"The rack accepts a title, a hat, and no additional RAM."},"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T13:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-20T13:00:00.000Z","section":"humor","status":"published","slug":"server-rack-middle-management"},
{"headline":"Skywatchers debate a daylight comet rumor","dek":"Astronomers say a viral orb is a weather balloon; horoscope desks still filed notes.","byline":"Sam Ortiz","desk":"Horoscope Desk","lede":"A daylight orb over the plains sent horoscope desks scrambling before astronomers called it a weather balloon with a shiny payload. The rumor still moved readers to ask what a false comet means for a week already packed with signs. We file the science and the sky notes in one place.","body":["Planetarium staff published a sun-angle chart that matches the viral clips.","Astrologers said the episode is about attention, not ice and dust.","Daily sign pages are overwritten each morning and are not archived in v1."],"hero":{"src":"/og/default.png","alt":"Horoscope news image"},"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T18:22:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T19:00:00.000Z","section":"horoscope","status":"published","slug":"daylight-comet-rumor"},
